            <ArticleTitle>Complete bipartition of the atlas in the Klippel-Feil syndrome. A radiologically illustrated case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with the Klippel-Feil syndrome is described who presented with pain in the neck after a trauma. No fractures were found. Instead, a midline cleft in both the anterior and posterior atlantic arches was found which represents an extremely rare congenital anomaly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
